e evidence mapping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-master-identity"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-master-identity"],"id":"long.thm-master-identity","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 5.14 (Decomposition of the integer remainder)","locator":"Long record Theorem 5.14, p. 41, label thm:master-identity","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For every quotient row $n \\ge 6$,\n$$\n\n\\Delta_n \\;=\\; K(2n) \\;+\\; \\sum_{d \\in \\mathrm{Skip}_n} \\left\\lfloor \\frac{4^n}{2^d-1} \\right\\rfloor.\n\\tag{I}\n$$\nHere the take and skip sets, capacity and remainder are those defined at the start of this subsection. The identity separates the contribution of the full exponent range from that of the omitted ranks. It makes no claim that there are few omitted ranks; controlling their sum is a separate part of any application.\\\n**Proof.** For $d=n$ the quotient is $2^n+1$, and for $n<d\\le2n$ it is $2^{2n-d}$. Hence\n$$\n\\sum_{d=n}^{2n}\\left\\lfloor\\frac{4^n}{2^d-1}\\right\\rfloor\n =2^n+1+\\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}2^j=2^{n+1}.\n$$\nSubstitute this in the definition of $K(2n)$, split $\\{2,\\ldots,n-1\\}=D_n\\sqcup\\mathrm{Skip}_n$, and use $\\Delta_n=2^{2n-1}-2^{n+1}-\\sum_{d\\in D_n}w(n,d)$. This gives (I). **Certification:** rows $6\\le n\\le200$ rechecked with zero mismatches by an exact [program](https://github.com/wcook04/plectis-erdos/blob/f757115e03bebe5c04431a147da559015c680a37/research/experiments/erdos257/check_master_identity.py) (§5.7).\\\n*Use:* (I) permits substitution of information about $K(2n)$. A resulting estimate for $\\Delta_n$ must also retain or bound the skip-set sum; information about $K$ alone need not control their cancellation.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-master-identity","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-master-identity","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-master-identity%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.paper_master_identity_floors%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-master-identity%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.paper_master_identity_floors%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.paper_master_identity_floors"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-master-identity","id":"field:76f97659ea858f52bc11383eee1794445479e4d99e19d8a1cacdbcd5df25afe4","kind":"evidence_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-master-identity","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"evidence_ids","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/evidence/mapping.long.thm-master-identity"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-master-identity","id":"field:8d2103094730251731a5a19ce025d8c34dafa3883ab686ba8688d91c74909b1e","kind":"source_id","owner_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-master-identity","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"source_id","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/sources/paper.long.pdf"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947a